From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:01:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 17/52] Message boxes as the console draws them
 (XamShowMessageBoxUI)

Games' and the dashboard's message boxes are xam's XuiMessageBox<n+1> in
the Guide frame's ErrorHUD, like the console: slid in over the dimmed
screen (ClosedToError), buttons stacked, up/down, A = the button, B = xam's
hidden cancel button (ERROR_CANCELLED), slid out (ErrorToClosed) before
the answer goes back. The frame and box come pre-rendered without texts
(guide/msgbox<n>_f<focus>.png from make_msgbox_assets.py, which also
records where each text and the icon go, msgbox.txt); the overlay composes
the title, message, buttons and icon (error/warning/alert) at run time in
the console font (XenonCLatin) with xui_render's text rules.

Passcode boxes and more than three buttons still use Xenia's dialog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
